  "_comment_preference": "frontier only. null, or {\"weights\": {metric_id: weight}}. With weights, sb/<id> points at the member with the largest weighted sum of normalized gains over the base f0; with null it points at the knee, the member whose smallest normalized gain over the base is largest, which is f0 itself until some member improves every goal. A decision aid for gate 2, not a claim (docs/13 §13.7).",
  "frontier_max": 8,
  "_comment_frontier_max": "frontier only. Most active members kept. Above it the member with the smallest NSGA-II crowding distance retires (retired_by: crowding); a member that is the extreme on some goal is pruned last. Every member keeps its branch sb/<id>-f<k>.",
